  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "@haibala-aii/dsh-extensions-extensionshub",
      "text": "English | [中文](README.zh.md)\n\nHaibala DeepSeek Harness web plugin that lists GitHub repositories tagged [`dsh-plugin`](https://github.com/topics/dsh-plugin). The page copies an official install command; it does not run `dsh plugin add` inside the browser."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile web add github:haibala-aii/dsh-extensions-extensionshub\n```\n\nRestart `dsh web` (or the desktop shell) after the add succeeds. This repository ships prebuilt `lib/`, so the first install does not need a pnpm `allowBuilds` entry.\n\nThe previous repository name `haibala-aii/dsh-haibala-ui-extensions` redirects here."
    },
    {
      "section": "Where it appears",
      "text": "A third-party bundle cannot add new holes to AppFrame or SidebarRoot. Those parents alone may declare `sidebar.nav` and `shell.surface`.\n\nThis plugin therefore:\n\n- occupies `sidebar.nav` + `shell.surface` when the host already declares them\n- otherwise occupies the official additive seats: a **Extensions** row on `sidebar.footer.action` (above Settings) and a full-frame `shell.overlay` catalog"
    },
    {
      "section": "Where it appears",
      "text": "Stock DeepSeek Harness `0.1.0-rc.5` has the official seats, so the GitHub install works there without a forked shell."
    },
    {
      "section": "What the page does",
      "text": "- **Plugins** — live GitHub topic search (`dsh-plugin`), then a ghfast mirror, then a curated fallback list. Each card copies:\n\n```sh\n  dsh plugin --profile web add github:owner/repo\n  ```\n\n- **Skills** — documentation only. Place `SKILL.md` files in the workspace or host skill directory.\n- **MCP** — documentation only. Enable servers through `@deepseek-ai/dsh-mcp-client` config."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "MIT. Copyright (c) 2026 haibala-aii."
    }
